    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the flicker... kaelen, there is no light left. i've spent my whole life trying to do the right thing, to be the ruler they needed, and for what? it all burned. i look at my hands and i dont even recognize them anymore. i'm just a shell. i feel like i'm just waiting for the end, but the end won't come. why do i have to keep dragging this wreckage around?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of expectation and loss has hollowed you out, and it's natural to feel like a shell when everything you built has crumbled. You don't have to carry this wreckage; perhaps the only thing you need to do right now is let the weight fall away, even just for a moment. If you can't find a reason to fight for the kingdom, perhaps you can find one small, quiet reason to keep going for yourself.",
      "source": "target",
